---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Fix DroidDeck Controller Not Detected — DroidDeck Guide"
  description="Fix controller detection and mapping issues in DroidDeck. Bluetooth, USB, and touch mapping tips."
  page="troubleshooting"

  locale="en"
>
  <style>
    .page-header{background:var(--night);color:white;padding:90px 0 50px}
    .page-header h1{font-size:36px;margin-bottom:12px}
    .page-header p{color:#93a7ba;max-width:600px}
    .page-content{padding:50px 0 80px;max-width:820px}
    .fix-section{margin-bottom:42px}
    .fix-section h2{font-size:24px;margin-bottom:14px}
    .fix-section p{font-size:15px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.9}
    .fix-section ol{padding-left:22px;font-size:15px;color:#43576c;line-height:1.9}
    .fix-section li{margin:10px 0}
    .callout{padding:16px 20px;background:#f0fdf4;border-left:4px solid #16a34a;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;margin:20px 0}
    .callout p{margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#166534;line-height:1.7}
    .tag-list{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:16px}
    .tag{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;padding:5px 12px;border-radius:999px;background:#f0f7fc;color:#147cb9}
  </style>
  
    <section class="page-header">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="hero-label"><span></span> Troubleshooting</div>
        <h1>Controller not detected / mapping issues</h1>
        <p>Bluetooth, USB, or built-in controller not working correctly inside DroidDeck.</p>
        <div class="tag-list">
          <span class="tag">Input</span>
          <span class="tag">Bluetooth</span>
          <span class="tag">Mapping</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-content wrap">
      <div class="fix-section">
        <h2>Step-by-step fixes</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Pair the controller before opening DroidDeck.</strong> Connect via Bluetooth or USB in Android settings first, then launch DroidDeck.</li>
          <li><strong>Use XInput-compatible controllers.</strong> Xbox, 8BitDo in X-input mode, and most modern gamepads work best. Some D-input only pads may not map correctly.</li>
          <li><strong>Check Steam controller settings.</strong> In Steam Big Picture, go to Settings → Controller and confirm your controller is detected.</li>
          <li><strong>Disable Steam Input for the game.</strong> Right-click the game → Properties → Controller → Disable Steam Input. This fixes many mapping issues.</li>
          <li><strong>Remap in DroidDeck's overlay.</strong> Use the touch controller editor to adjust on-screen buttons, or reassign physical buttons if needed.</li>
          >li><strong>Try a wired connection.</strong> If Bluetooth latency or detection is unreliable, use a USB-C cable or adapter.</li>
          <li><strong>Restart after sleep.</strong> Some devices lose controller input after sleep. Fully close and reopen DroidDeck.</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="callout">
          <p>Built-in handheld controllers usually work out of the box. If buttons are swapped (e.g., A/B), check Steam's controller configuration for your region's button layout.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="fix-section">
        <h2>Still stuck?</h2>
        <p>Tell us your controller model, connection type (BT/USB), whether Steam sees it, and whether the issue is in menus, in-game, or both.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  
  
</Layout>
